{"instruction": "Write a function `int_to_roman(n)` returning the Roman numeral for 1..3999. Example: `int_to_roman(3)`.", "response": "def int_to_roman(n):\n    pairs = [(1000,'M'),(900,'CM'),(500,'D'),(400,'CD'),\n             (100,'C'),(90,'XC'),(50,'L'),(40,'XL'),\n             (10,'X'),(9,'IX'),(5,'V'),(4,'IV'),(1,'I')]\n    out = ''\n    for v, s in pairs:\n        while n >= v:\n            out += s\n            n -= v\n    return out\n"}
